Bite Attacks
Vampires can use their fangs as
weapons during a Brawl-based attack.
To attempt a bite attack, the
player must declare their intention
to bite before rolling their
dice and remove two dice from
their pool – bite attacks are easier
to defend against and harder to
target on exposed flesh.
Regardless of the number of
successes rolled, vampire fangs do
two points of damage with a win on
the Brawl roll. Fangs deal Aggravated
Health damage to mortals and vampires.
On turns following a successful bite attack, the vampire can feed from the
target. At this point, the vampire suffers no penalty to their Brawl pool – a successful
bite is hard to dislodge. Feeding does one point of Aggravated Health
damage to mortals per turn as well as slake 1 Hunger for the feeder. Against
a vampire target, a feeding attack increases the target’s Hunger by 1 per turn,
