do you do?”
If you have not
asked this question
in a while, it is probably
a sign there is not
enough stuff in your
game for the players to
react to.
The Scene
Every individual game session in your chronicle has
to start with a specific situation. The characters are
somewhere, doing something. The situation does not
necessarily have to be dramatic. They can be at their
haven, playing pool. The important thing is to get the
players inside their characters from the first minutes
of play. Typically, it is a good idea to have something
interesting happen at to get things moving. Maybe a
supporting character comes to visit, bearing surprising
news. Maybe a dear friend of one of the characters has
disappeared. As long as the players get something to
react to.
