artistic performance
Vampires are egotistical monsters
even when they weren’t performers
in life. When a character performs
live before an audience, roll
Charisma + Performance: the more
successes, the greater the quality.
Just as with artistic creation,
always indicate the purpose behind
the roll. On a total failure, the
performance was a total disaster –
and the performer may have new
enemies among the Toreador they
didn’t have when they woke up this
evening.
carousing
With a simple test of Charisma
+ Insight, you influence others
(particularly potential vessels) to
relax and have fun. Carousing encompasses
showing a potential ally
a good time, loosening an informant’s
tongue, and making instant
drinking buddies who come to
your aid when a brawl starts.
Vampires who can’t drink (most
of them) may lose one or two dice
from this roll (or have to make a
sleight of hand test (p. 415) to fake
it), depending on how important
sharing a beer or the equivalent is
to the subject.
credibility
Flashing a phony ID and brushing
past the rope line, perpetrating a
scam or con, presenting false credentials
to get a job, passing counterfeit
artifacts, impersonating the
authorities – tests of credibility
take many forms. The scammer
uses Manipulation + Subterfuge;
the mark rolls Wits + Insight.
Storytellers and players interested
in running a long con can set
a suitably impressive Difficulty and
play out an extended test.
Superior fake documents and
other forgeries add dice (an addiAPPENDIX
